---
title: Memory across voice and text - one session, two trust levels
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as Customer (demo: Omar)
    participant IN as Transport (voice / text)
    participant S as SupportService
    participant M as Session memory (process-local)
    participant R as HybridRouter
    participant OT as Order tools

    rect rgb(246, 250, 250)
        Note over U,OT: Turn 1 · voice
        U->>IN: "Where is order NS-26-2044-8?" (audio)
        IN->>S: handle(transcript, session="demo-session-omar", channel="voice")
        S->>M: snapshot → no verified slots yet
        S->>R: route → Tier 0 rule: one order ID + an order operation
        S->>OT: get_order_status(NS-26-2044-8, session)
        OT-->>S: delivered September 25, 2026 · owner verified
        S->>M: append voice turn · active_order = NS-26-2044-8 · active_product = CityHaul 20
        S-->>U: "Your CityHaul 20 backpack (order NS-26-2044-8) was delivered on September 25, 2026." (TTS)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 240)
        Note over U,OT: Turn 2 · text, same session
        U->>IN: "Can I return it?"
        IN->>S: handle(text, session="demo-session-omar", channel="text")
        S->>M: snapshot → active_order = NS-26-2044-8
        S->>R: route → Tier 0 rule: pronoun + order action + verified order (no LLM call)
        S->>OT: check_return_eligibility(NS-26-2044-8, session)
        OT-->>S: eligible · Trail Week window · deadline November 15, 2026
        S->>M: append text turn
        S-->>U: "Good news: … can be returned … The return deadline is November 15, 2026. Return eligibility is not a refund approval."
    end

    rect rgb(246, 250, 250)
        Note over U,OT: Turn 3 · text
        U->>IN: "Talk to a human"
        IN->>S: handle(text, same session)
        S->>R: route → Tier 0 rule: explicit request for a person
        S->>M: handoff_summary() → verified slots + last six voice and text turns
        S-->>U: "I've passed this conversation to a human support agent. Your reference is HO-…"
    end

    Note over S,M: Only verified slots ever reach an LLM. The transcript feeds the handoff summary and is never placed in a prompt.
